{%- comment -%}
  Veylin's design system, rendered by the theme itself.

  Reach it at /pages/<any-page>?view=design-system, or assign the template to
  a page in admin. It is developer-facing: every string here is literal English
  on purpose, because translating a page no shopper sees would put ~90 keys in
  every locale a merchant has to maintain.

  Two jobs:

  1. It is the one place the whole system is visible at once. A token that
     changes shows up here, next to every other token it has to live with.
  2. It is the visual-regression surface. Diff this page across a change and
     anything unintended has to explain itself — which is what the theme's
     invariant asks for, and what the section pages cannot give you, since a
     homepage exercises maybe a third of the tokens.

  It reads the *computed* values rather than the settings, so what it prints is
  what the browser actually resolved — not what Liquid meant to emit. That
  distinction is the entire point: the footer padding bug, the container query
  that never fired and the 0px scroll region were all correct in source.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Styled here rather than in base.css on purpose: this page is developer
  tooling, and shipping its ~70 lines to every shopper on every template would
  be paying for it forever to serve nobody. The theme's own tokens do the work;
  these rules only lay the specimens out.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .ds { padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-3xl); }
  .ds__head { margin-block-end: var(--space-2xl); }
  .ds__block { margin-block-start: var(--space-3xl); }
  .ds__block > .h2 { margin-block-end: var(--space-sm); }
  .ds__block > .rte { margin-block-end: var(--space-lg); }

  .ds__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 18rem) 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    align-items: baseline;
    padding-block: var(--space-2xs);
    border-block-end: var(--border-width) solid var(--c-hairline);
  }
  .ds__key {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--c-muted);
    word-break: break-all;
  }
  .ds__key--empty { color: var(--c-error); font-weight: 700; }
  .ds__row > span:last-child {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--c-text);
  }

  .ds__scheme { padding: var(--space-lg); margin-block-end: var(--space-md); }
  .ds__scheme-name { margin-block-end: var(--space-sm); }
  .ds__swatches {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(10rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .ds__swatch { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; min-width: 0; }
  .ds__chip {
    inline-size: 1.75rem;
    block-size: 1.75rem;
    flex: none;
    border: var(--border-width) solid var(--c-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  .ds__swatch-name {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--c-muted);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .ds__scheme-demo { margin-block-start: var(--space-md); }

  .ds__steps { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: var(--space-md); flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .ds__step { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .ds__bar {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 3rem;
    min-block-size: 2px;
    background: var(--c-accent);
  }
  .ds__step-val {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    color: var(--c-muted);
    text-align: center;
    max-inline-size: 7rem;
  }

  .ds__motion { display: flex; gap: var(--space-md); margin-block-end: var(--space-lg); }
  .ds__tile {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    inline-size: 9rem;
    block-size: 5rem;
    background: var(--c-surface);
    border: var(--border-width) solid var(--c-hairline);
    font-size: var(--micro-size);
    letter-spacing: var(--micro-tracking);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .ds__tile--ui { transition: transform var(--duration) var(--ease-ui), background var(--duration) var(--ease-ui); }
  .ds__tile--entrance { transition: transform calc(var(--duration) * 2) var(--ease), background calc(var(--duration) * 2) var(--ease); }
  .ds__tile:hover { transform: translateY(-10px); background: var(--c-accent); }

  .ds__buttons {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin-block: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-lg);
  }
  .ds__ink { padding: var(--space-lg); margin-block-start: var(--space-sm); }
  .ds__loaders { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-xl); }

  .ds__marks { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-lg); flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .ds__mark { display: inline-flex; padding: var(--space-sm); }
  .ds__mark svg { inline-size: 3rem; block-size: auto; }
  .ds__mark--ink { color: var(--c-champagne); }
</style>

<div class="page-width ds">
  <header class="ds__head">
    <div class="micro">Veylin design system</div>
    <h1 class="display">The system, rendered by the theme</h1>
    <p class="section-lede">
      Every value below is read back from the browser, not from the schema.
      Resize the window — everything fluid is meant to move.
    </p>
  </header>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Emblem -------------------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ds__block">
    <h2 class="h2">Emblem</h2>
    <p class="rte measure">
      Inline SVG on <code>currentColor</code>, so it takes the colour of the
      surface it sits on — which is what the two PNG cuts it replaced were
      faking. It only appears in the lockup when the wordmark has a repeated
      letter to stand in for; "VEYLIN" has none, which is why the homepage
      shows no emblem today.
    </p>
    <div class="ds__marks">
      <span class="ds__mark">{%- render 'wordmark-mark' -%}</span>
      <span class="ds__mark" style="color: var(--c-accent)">{%- render 'wordmark-mark' -%}</span>
      <span class="ds__mark ds__mark--ink scheme-scheme_2">{%- render 'wordmark-mark' -%}</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Brand palette ------------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ds__block">
    <h2 class="h2">Brand palette</h2>
    <p class="rte measure">
      The seven constants the design names. None of them is a colour picker of
      its own — the light three are read from the page scheme and the dark four
      from whichever scheme is nominated as the dark one, so changing a scheme
      changes every surface built from it.
    </p>
    <div class="ds__swatches">
      {%- assign brand = 'porcelain,ink,gold,noir,noir-surface,ivory,champagne,noir-deep,error' | split: ',' -%}
      {%- for b in brand -%}
        <div class="ds__swatch">
          <span class="ds__chip" style="background: var(--c-{{ b }})"></span>
          <span class="ds__swatch-name" data-ds-var="--c-{{ b }}">--c-{{ b }}</span>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Colour schemes ------------------------------------ {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ds__block">
    <h2 class="h2">Colour schemes</h2>
    <p class="rte measure">Each scheme sets its own text, surface and accent, and derives its hairline, shadow and veil from its own literal colours rather than from <code>:root</code>.</p>
    {%- for scheme in settings.color_schemes -%}
      <div class="ds__scheme scheme-{{ scheme.id }}">
        <div class="ds__scheme-name micro">{{ scheme.id }}</div>
        <div class="ds__swatches">
          {%- assign roles = 'bg,text,heading,muted,accent,border,surface,button,button-label,link,hairline,shadow' | split: ',' -%}
          {%- for role in roles -%}
            <div class="ds__swatch">
              <span class="ds__chip" style="background: var(--c-{{ role }})"></span>
              <span class="ds__swatch-name" data-ds-var="--c-{{ role }}">--c-{{ role }}</span>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
        <p class="ds__scheme-demo">Body copy in this scheme, with <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">a link</a> and <em>emphasis</em>.</p>
      </div>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Type ---------------------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ds__block">
    <h2 class="h2">Type scale</h2>
    <p class="rte measure">Nine fluid steps interpolated between 360 and 1440, plus two art-directed heading scales of their own.</p>
    <div class="ds__type">
      {%- assign steps = 'xs,sm,base,md,lg,xl,2xl,3xl,4xl' | split: ',' -%}
      {%- for s in steps -%}
        <div class="ds__row">
          <code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="--fs-{{ s }}">--fs-{{ s }}</code>
          <span style="font-size: var(--fs-{{ s }}); line-height: 1.2">Veylin</span>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
      <div class="ds__row">
        <code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="--fs-section">--fs-section</code>
        <span class="h2">Section heading</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ds__row">
        <code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="--fs-display">--fs-display</code>
        <span class="display">Display</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Spacing steps ------------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ds__block">
    <h2 class="h2">Spacing steps</h2>
    <p class="rte measure">
      The rungs a merchant picks from for section padding. Every one is fluid and
      no two are alike at any width — the bars below should never match, at any
      window size.
    </p>
    <div class="ds__steps">
      {%- assign rungs = 'none,2xs,xs,sm,md,lg,xl,max' | split: ',' -%}
      {%- for r in rungs -%}
        {%- capture v -%}{%- render 'space-step', step: r -%}{%- endcapture -%}
        <div class="ds__step">
          <code class="ds__key">{{ r }}</code>
          <span class="ds__bar" style="height: {{ v }}"></span>
          <span class="ds__step-val" data-ds-measure="bar">{{ v }}</span>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Motion -------------------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ds__block">
    <h2 class="h2">Motion</h2>
    <p class="rte measure">
      Two registers. <code>--ease-ui</code> is plain <code>ease</code> and belongs to
      interaction; <code>--ease</code> is the entrance curve and belongs to things
      arriving. Hover the tiles.
    </p>
    <div class="ds__motion">
      <div class="ds__tile ds__tile--ui"><span>--ease-ui</span></div>
      <div class="ds__tile ds__tile--entrance"><span>--ease</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ds__row"><code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="--duration">--duration</code><span></span></div>
    <div class="ds__row"><code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="--ease-ui">--ease-ui</code><span></span></div>
    <div class="ds__row"><code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="--ease">--ease</code><span></span></div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Buttons ------------------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ds__block">
    <h2 class="h2">Buttons</h2>
    <p class="rte measure">
      The design's own four, plus its stepped-back link and its arrow carrying
      the outline's frame. Every one is a real <code>snippets/button.liquid</code>
      render, so what is below is what a section emits. Hover the arrows —
      the gap travels 11px to 19px on the long ease-out.
    </p>

    <div class="micro">Style</div>
    <div class="ds__buttons">
      {%- assign ds_styles = 'filled,outline,link,quiet,arrow,arrow_outline' | split: ',' -%}
      {%- for st in ds_styles -%}
        {%- render 'button', label: st, link: routes.all_products_collection_url, style: st -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" disabled>Disabled</button>
    </div>

    <div class="micro">Size — per button, overriding the theme setting</div>
    <div class="ds__buttons">
      {%- assign ds_sizes = 'xs,sm,md,lg,xl' | split: ',' -%}
      {%- for sz in ds_sizes -%}
        {%- render 'button', label: sz, link: routes.all_products_collection_url, style: 'filled', size: sz -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    <div class="micro">Shape — per button, overriding the theme setting</div>
    <div class="ds__buttons">
      {%- assign ds_radii = 'square,soft,rounded,pill' | split: ',' -%}
      {%- for rd in ds_radii -%}
        {%- render 'button', label: rd, link: routes.all_products_collection_url, style: 'outline', radius: rd -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    <div class="micro">Card and full-width</div>
    <div class="ds__buttons">
      <a class="btn btn--square" href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">Square (in-card)</a>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      "Same four, inverted for dark bands and the atelier footer" — the design's
      own note. It is a scheme, not six more variants, so the specimens below
      are the identical renders inside a dark colour scheme.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="micro">On ink — the same four, in a dark scheme</div>
    <div class="ds__ink scheme-scheme_2">
      <div class="ds__buttons">
        {%- for st in ds_styles -%}
          {%- render 'button', label: st, link: routes.all_products_collection_url, style: st -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ds__row"><code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="--button-radius">--button-radius</code><span></span></div>
    <div class="ds__row"><code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="--button-padding-x">--button-padding-x</code><span></span></div>
    <div class="ds__row"><code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="--button-padding-y">--button-padding-y</code><span></span></div>
    <div class="ds__row"><code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="--button-size">--button-size</code><span></span></div>
    <div class="ds__row"><code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="--button-tracking">--button-tracking</code><span></span></div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Shape and layout ---------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ds__block">
    <h2 class="h2">Shape and layout</h2>
    <div class="ds__type">
      {%- assign shape = '--radius,--radius-sm,--radius-arch,--border-width,--hairline,--shadow-strength,--page-width,--page-width-narrow,--content-width,--gutter,--grid-min,--grid-gap,--micro-size,--micro-tracking,--body-leading,--heading-leading,--display-leading,--display-tracking' | split: ',' -%}
      {%- for t in shape -%}
        <div class="ds__row"><code class="ds__key" data-ds-var="{{ t }}">{{ t }}</code><span></span></div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---- The product card ---------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ds__block">
    <h2 class="h2">Product card</h2>
    <p class="rte measure">The real snippet, so its caption type, swatch row and framing are checked here rather than only on the homepage.</p>
    {%- assign ds_collection = collections.all -%}
    <div class="grid-auto grid-auto--products">
      {%- for product in ds_collection.products limit: 4 -%}
        {%- render 'product-card', product: product -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- render 'product-card' -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Loading mark -------------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ds__block">
    <h2 class="h2">Loading</h2>
    <div class="ds__loaders">
      {%- render 'loader', size: 'sm' -%}
      {%- render 'loader', size: 'md' -%}
      {%- render 'loader', size: 'lg' -%}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  Values are filled in by script rather than by Liquid, because Liquid can only
  print what it *meant* to emit. A custom property that resolves to nothing —
  the failure this theme keeps meeting — looks identical in the source and
  blank on the page. Reading it back is the only way the page can tell you.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    var root = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-ds-var]').forEach(function (el) {
      var name = el.getAttribute('data-ds-var');
      var scope = el.closest('[class*="scheme-"]') || document.documentElement;
      var val = getComputedStyle(scope).getPropertyValue(name).trim() || root.getPropertyValue(name).trim();
      var out = el.nextElementSibling;
      var text = val || '(unresolved)';
      /* Some rows keep a live specimen in the value slot — a line of type set
         in the size being named — so the resolved value goes onto the key
         itself rather than overwriting what it is there to demonstrate. */
      if (out && out.tagName === 'SPAN' && !out.textContent.trim()) out.textContent = text;
      else el.textContent = name + '  ' + text;
      el.setAttribute('title', text);
      if (!val) el.classList.add('ds__key--empty');
    });
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-ds-measure="bar"]').forEach(function (el) {
      var bar = el.previousElementSibling;
      if (bar) el.textContent = el.textContent.trim() + '  =  ' + Math.round(bar.getBoundingClientRect().height) + 'px';
    });
  })();
</script>
